.SS CVE\-2019\-15752
Docker Desktop Community Edition, added 2021\-11\-03.
.PP
Docker Desktop Community Edition Privilege Escalation Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Docker Desktop Community Edition contains a vulnerability that may allow local users to escalate privileges by placing a trojan horse docker\-credential\-wincred.exe file in %PROGRAMDATA%\eDockerDesktop\eversion\-bin\e.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2022\-05\-03.
.PP
\fIReferences:\fR
.br
https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE\-2019\-15752
.SS CVE\-2026\-123039
Check Point Multiple Products, added 2026\-11\-13.
.PP
Check Point Multiple Products Incorrect Permission Assignment for Critical Resource Vulnerability.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Check Point Firewall, Multi\-Domain Security Management Server, Scalable Platforms, Security Gateway, and Security Management Server contain an incorrect permissions assignment for critical resources vulnerability when the Gaia OS DynamicCLI daemon runs as root and listens on a world\-writable local socket without authenticating connecting processes. An authenticated local user can send a command to the socket and have it executed as root.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply vendor mitigations; follow CISA BOD 26\-04 (risk\-based patching) and forensics triage. Discontinue use if no mitigation exists.
 Due 2026\-11\-16.
.PP
